&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring Ranges:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Remote UK&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£66,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£87,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2 class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Company Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ecosio is a fast-growing, innovative service company and a leading provider of B2B integration, specialising in electronic data interchange (EDI), Web EDI and e-invoicing. ecosio is part of Vertex, Inc., a leading global provider of indirect tax solutions listed on Nasdaq (VERX).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our brand slogan is&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Connections That Work&lt;/em&gt; as we believe strong connections are central to successful business relationships - both external and internal. At ecosio, we hire individuals from all backgrounds and are committed to creating an inclusive work environment. We are technology lovers, set the highest standards for our solutions, and put innovative ideas first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Job Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Product Owner to own our workflow platform end to end, make bold decisions and ship AI-native automation that transforms how ecosio works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll connect with the role if you enjoy:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Having the freedom and accountability to challenge existing processes, prototype quickly and drive ideas through to company-wide adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking ambiguous workflow problems from first insight to shipped solution and measurable impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritizing features and enhancements based on business impact and user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing intuitive user interfaces and experiences for internal applications with AI workflows in mind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working directly with teams to uncover high-leverage problems and turn them into clear product bets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducting user training sessions and creating interactive documentation for clear user enablement and feature adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyzing usage data to identify optimization opportunities, adoption and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating daily with UI/UX designers and engineering teams to prototype, test, and ship high-impact tooling functionality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To connect with ecosio, it is important to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–4 years of experience in product management or a related role, preferably in a SaaS environment (e.g. Project Management software, Configuration systems, Agent systems)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Native Expertise&lt;/strong&gt; - an understanding of modern AI/ML technology (e.g. LLMs, RAGs, MCPs, agentic systems and other concepts) and ability to demonstrate how you build or optimize features and workflows with AI tools in your work or side projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in a dynamic, evolving environment, embracing new priorities and challenges as opportunities to learn and grow. Curiosity, adaptability, disciplined execution and strategic communication are part of your core values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong product vision and the ability to break the the big picture into small, shippable, impactful increments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mindset focused on how users think, ensuring our products and workflow tools are intuitive, efficient, and user-friendly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with agent building, prototyping/design tools, documentation/planning tools, ticketing systems, and analytics tools (e.g. Figma, Posthog,…)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And nice to have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A technical background or education (HTL, FH, university,..)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in workflow automation, process improvement, or configuring complex transactional systems/logs (e.g., document exchange or fintech)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of EDI concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Additional Information&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By connecting with us you will experience...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our remote-first culture lets you work remotely from one of our designated countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours to suit your schedule and priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual personal development budget to invest in conferences, courses, or career coaching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office allowance to create a workspace that fits your needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular events and trips to connect, celebrate, and have fun with the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workations of up to 90 days per year within the EU, combining travel and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellbeing support, including mental health resources and employee assistance programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional country-specific benefits based on your location&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sounds like a connection that works? Then apply now and we will get in touch soon!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to build Connections That Work by fostering a diverse and inclusive team. We are committed to making everyone feel valued and empowered to contribute their unique skills, experiences and perspectives. And now we want to connect with you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use Metaview Notetaker to support interview documentation during our recruiting process. Further information on the processing of personal data can be found in our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ecosio.com/en/data-protection/&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of our hiring process at ecosio, we conduct standard background checks. You can find more information about them by clicking&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ecosio.com/en/background-check/&quot;&gt;HERE&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Parloa&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Parloa’s mission is to make every customer conversation feel effortless for both customers and the companies serving them. As agentic AI accelerates, Parloans are shaping the foundation of a new era in customer experience, one where customer support is no longer transactions, but meaningful exchanges. It is not just a vision; Parloa has powered over ONE BILLION interactions between global enterprise brands and their customers, with companies like &lt;a href=&quot;http://booking.com&quot;&gt;Booking.com&lt;/a&gt;, HealthEquity, Allianz, SAP, BarmeniaGothaer, and TUI already deploying Parloa at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Staff Product Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, you will work directly inside our most strategic enterprise customers. You will build the software that makes their AI agents work in production, and be measured by the difference it makes for the customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our agents are built by business users in Parloa’s platform, AMP. AMP already comes with a broad library of tools and integrations. Your job is the part AMP does not cover yet for a given customer: the last connection into their systems, or a capability the product does not have. Our customers are large enterprises in financial services, telecom, insurance, travel and retail. For them, a working prototype is where an engagement starts, not where it ends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The work comes in two forms. Some engagements run for years. You stay with the account, deepen its integrations and help it grow into new use cases. Others are short experiments. You test a new idea with a real customer and decide quickly whether it is worth building. At Staff level, you take on the hardest cases of both: accounts where a pilot-grade solution would fail in production, and capabilities nobody at Parloa has built before. Staff means harder problems and more ambiguity, not less hands-on work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On many accounts, you work alongside a Deployment Strategist. Think of the two of you as the account’s leadership team. The Deployment Strategist acts as its CPO and defines what success looks like. You act as its CTO and own the architecture and the build. On accounts without a Deployment Strategist, you own the engineering yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Areas of ownership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the hardest engagements.&lt;/strong&gt; Run complex programmes with several workstreams. Make the architecture decisions that span Parloa’s platform and several parts of the customer’s organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build what AMP does not cover yet.&lt;/strong&gt; Systems of record, telephony and contact-center integrations, state management, data readiness, multi-agent orchestration and retrieval. When the answer is unclear, build a prototype quickly and decide whether it is worth pursuing before Parloa invests a full quarter in it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own production quality and security.&lt;/strong&gt; Evals, production readiness, observability and incident playbooks for enterprise-scale traffic. Meet the data handling standards a regulated customer expects, including PII, access control and audit trails. Debug live issues, whether they are technical or caused by model behaviour.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow the account, and share what belongs in the product.&lt;/strong&gt; Drive the second use case, the second business unit, the renewal. Set the delivery standard for other engineers on complex accounts. When something you build would help every customer, flag it. That is how Parloa decides what goes into the core product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentor other Product Engineers&lt;/strong&gt;, and take part in interviewing and hiring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use AI well, and set the standard for it.&lt;/strong&gt; Decide how AI-assisted work is validated before it reaches a customer’s production traffic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Represent Parloa with senior technical stakeholders.&lt;/strong&gt; Work directly with the customer’s principal engineers, architects and security leaders. Be the engineer commercial teams bring in when a prospect asks how the solution would work for them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What this role is not:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not running the Parloa platform itself.&lt;/strong&gt; That is a separate engineering role. The platform is your foundation, and you build what a specific customer needs on top of it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not agent configuration.&lt;/strong&gt; Business users design and configure agents in AMP. You build the integrations and capabilities those agents need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not a people-management role.&lt;/strong&gt; You are an individual contributor and write and review code every week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OUR TECH STACK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Go, TypeScript, Node.js, Python, FastAPI, frontier LLMs, MCP, Azure, Kubernetes, Docker, Terraform, MongoDB, Redis, Kafka/NATS&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will not use all of these, and most engagements add something new.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years of professional software development&lt;/strong&gt;, delivering production systems end to end. Fluent in TypeScript or Python, or able to get there quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years leading the design and architecture of large-scale production systems&lt;/strong&gt; in customer-facing or enterprise environments, with a focus on reliability, scale and failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience leading agentic, spec-driven development in production.&lt;/strong&gt; You know when a coding agent’s output is wrong and what checks it needs before it ships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A track record in long-term accounts or fast experiments.&lt;/strong&gt; You have owned a strategic enterprise relationship over several years, through an expansion, a renewal or a leadership change. Or you have tested new ideas at the frontier and decided quickly whether they were worth building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience as a mentor or tech lead&lt;/strong&gt;, helping engineers become independent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity and with customers.&lt;/strong&gt; You work well in complex organizations, build trust quickly with new customer teams, spot risks early and keep your judgment when the stakes are high.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Willingness to travel up to 25%&lt;/strong&gt; to customer sites, depending on the engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong spoken and written communication skills in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or deploying an LLM-powered system used by real users in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with eval frameworks, agent tooling, RAG, prompt engineering or multi-agent orchestration (few candidates will have all of these)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A founder or founding-engineer background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forward-deployed, solutions engineering, product engineering or strategic-partner experience at an enterprise software or AI company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voice or conversational AI, or contact center, telephony or CCaaS integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in regulated industries such as banking, insurance or telecom&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our engineering values:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Parloa, we hire, promote, and evaluate based on cultural and technical excellence. You’ll thrive here if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Earn Trust&lt;/strong&gt; – act with transparency and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Obsess Over Customers&lt;/strong&gt; – always start with the customer problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think Big&lt;/strong&gt; – set bold goals and pursue them fearlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Have Integrity&lt;/strong&gt; – do the right thing, especially when it’s hard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disagree &amp;amp; Commit&lt;/strong&gt; – debate with candor, align fast, and deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own It&lt;/strong&gt; – take full responsibility for outcomes, not just tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dive Deep&lt;/strong&gt; – master the details without losing sight of the big picture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias for Action&lt;/strong&gt; – move fast, decide quickly, iterate fearlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver Value&lt;/strong&gt; – measure success by customer and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insist on the Highest Standards&lt;/strong&gt; – raise the bar continuously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go the Extra Mile&lt;/strong&gt; – make the impossible possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hire &amp;amp; Elevate the Best&lt;/strong&gt; – raise the bar with every hire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our recruiting process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recruiter Call → Technical Peer Interview → 360° Tech Interview Loop → Bar Raiser&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Parloa?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re at the beginning of a new era in customer experience, one where AI doesn’t just respond, but understands, reasons, and takes action. We’re building agentic AI that enterprises trust with their most important customer moments: complex questions, high volumes, real stakes. When millions of people reach out to a brand, those interactions aren’t just support tickets; they’re defining experiences. We’re here to raise the standard: making every conversation seamless, intelligent, and genuinely helpful. If you care about shaping how businesses and customers connect at scale—and want your work to matter in real, everyday moments—this is where you do it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Parloa, ownership isn’t a buzzword; it means being accountable for outcomes, not just tasks. We operate in a category that’s evolving fast, where the bar is high, and the problems are complex. We hire people who think in solutions, communicate with clarity, and follow through. People who are comfortable making decisions, taking responsibility, and raising the standard for themselves and those around them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve grown beyond the earliest startup phase, but we’ve kept the intensity: fast execution, direct feedback, and a strong expectation to contribute meaningfully from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading global investors like General Catalyst, EQT Ventures, and Altimeter Capital, we’re scaling with a clear ambition: to become the global category leader in enterprise-grade conversational AI.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;display: table; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/P4d-iyx7RQM&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Parloa is committed to upholding the highest data protection standards for our clients&#39; and employees&#39; data. All our employees are instrumental in ensuring the utmost care, GDPR, and ISO compliance, including ISO 27001, in handling sensitive information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Parloa is an e-verify employer in the USA. &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/about-e-verify/what-is-e-verify&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/about-e-verify/what-is-e-verify&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Please click here to learn more&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;* &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We provide equal opportunities to all qualified applicants regardless race, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, national origin, disability status, socioeconomic background and other characteristics.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you passionate about uncovering meaningful user insights and influencing product decisions through evidence-based research?  We&#39;re looking for a Senior UX Researcher to lead strategic and tactical research initiatives across our platform, helping teams better understand our customers and make informed decisions with confidence.  You&#39;ll partner closely with Product, Design, Engineering, Data, and other customer facing teams to plan and deliver impactful research. You&#39;ll be comfortable navigating ambiguity, balancing multiple priorities, and driving research projects forward from inception to outcome with minimal oversight.  Our team is a group of collaborative, curious, and dedicated people who care deeply about creating great experiences for our customers. Alongside meaningful work, we offer a supportive environment and a range of excellent benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be responsible for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading end-to-end research projects, from problem definition and scoping through to synthesis, recommendations, and stakeholder alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Planning and executing a range of qualitative and quantitative research activities, including usability testing, interviews, surveys, workshops, and behavioural analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translating complex research findings into clear, actionable insights that drive product and business decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing multiple research initiatives simultaneously, balancing competing priorities while maintaining quality and momentum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating closely with Product, Design, Engineering, Customer Success, and Commercial teams to identify research opportunities and answer high-value business questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicating research findings confidently and effectively to a range of audiences, from practitioners to senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influencing product strategy through evidence-based recommendations and championing customer needs across the organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helping teams navigate ambiguity by identifying research approaches, defining next steps, and bringing clarity to complex problem spaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the development of research operations, processes, tooling, and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining and contributing to our insights repository to ensure research findings are accessible and reusable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentoring colleagues and supporting the continued growth of research maturity across the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building strong relationships with stakeholders to establish effective feedback loops and strengthen the voice of the customer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years&#39; experience conducting UX Research within digital products or related fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of qualitative and quantitative research methodologies and when to use them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in independently leading complex research projects from start to finish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in ambiguous environments and able to bring structure and&amp;nbsp;direction to unclear problem spaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, facilitation, and presentation skills, with the ability to tailor messages for different audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at synthesising large volumes of information into clear narratives, insights,&amp;nbsp;and recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident engaging with stakeholders, challenging assumptions constructively, and influencing decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to prioritise effectively across multiple projects, balancing business goals, customer needs, and team capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage several concurrent workstreams while maintaining a high standard of delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive, self-sufficient, and comfortable identifying and resolving blockers independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational skills with excellent attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious, analytical, and motivated to understand the &quot;why&quot; behind customer behaviour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about creating user-centred products and embedding customer insight into decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role would suit someone who thrives in a fast-moving environment, enjoys solving complex problems, and can confidently drive research forward, even when the path ahead isn&#39;t fully defined&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;RichTextList-bulleted&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;TypographyPresentation TypographyPresentation--medium RichText3-paragraph--withVSpacingNormal RichText3-paragraph HighlightSol HighlightSol--buildingBlock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexi-Week&lt;/strong&gt;: We prioritise your mental health and wellbeing by offering you a four-day Flexi-Week (with one lighter or completely disconnected day per week) at full pay, with no reduction to your annual holiday allowance.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;TypographyPresentation TypographyPresentation--medium RichText3-paragraph--withVSpacingNormal RichText3-paragraph HighlightSol HighlightSol--buildingBlock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexi-office&lt;/strong&gt;: We offer an international culture and flexibility through our hybrid/remote working scheme which is designed to foster a culture of mutual trust and working flexibility.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;TypographyPresentation TypographyPresentation--medium RichText3-paragraph--withVSpacingNormal RichText3-paragraph HighlightSol HighlightSol--buildingBlock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Expense Contribution &amp;amp; Remote Working Furniture&lt;/strong&gt;: You will receive a monthly allowance to cover part of your running costs, as well as a furniture package to support you in setting up a comfortable workspace when working from home.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;TypographyPresentation TypographyPresentation--medium RichText3-paragraph--withVSpacingNormal RichText3-paragraph HighlightSol HighlightSol--buildingBlock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health and Wellbeing&lt;/strong&gt;: With our support and access to various initiatives and sports offers, you can focus on your mental and physical wellbeing.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;TypographyPresentation TypographyPresentation--medium RichText3-paragraph--withVSpacingNormal RichText3-paragraph HighlightSol HighlightSol--buildingBlock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Development&lt;/strong&gt;: We’ve built our extensive training suite, Awin Academy, to cover a wide range of skills that support your professional and personal growth, with trainings conveniently packaged to help your overall development.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;TypographyPresentation TypographyPresentation--medium RichText3-paragraph--withVSpacingNormal RichText3-paragraph HighlightSol HighlightSol--buildingBlock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Appreciation&lt;/strong&gt;: Thank and reward colleagues by sending them a voucher through our peer-to-peer recognition programme.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;TypographyPresentation TypographyPresentation--medium RichText3-paragraph--withVSpacingNormal RichText3-paragraph HighlightSol HighlightSol--buildingBlock&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are hiring in multiple countries for this role. Additional benefits, including health and wellbeing offerings, will be discussed during the initial interview.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Established in 2000, Awin is proud of our dynamic, social and inclusive culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Like all businesses, we’ve had to adapt and nurture our culture in a virtual environment. Our virtual ‘Life @ Awin’ hub brings our colleagues from across the globe together for various social activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Diversity &amp;amp; Inclusion are paramount to us, and we proudly pursue and hire diverse team members. We champion uniqueness and authenticity; this is who we are at our core. Our network of affiliate partnerships are diverse and transparent, as are the employees powering our vision to build the world’s leading open partner ecosystem. We welcome all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. If you need support at any point in the application or interview process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun Highlight SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot;&gt;Awin is part of the Axel Springer group.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;TextRun Highlight SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot;&gt;Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;Hyperlink SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; href=&quot;https://www.axelspringer.com/en/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun Highlight Underlined SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;axelspringer.com/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;en&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun Highlight SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot;&gt;, and explore the Axel Springer Essentials here:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a class=&quot;Hyperlink SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; href=&quot;https://www.axelspringer.com/en/inside/the-essentials-what-we-have-adapted-and-why&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun Highlight Underlined SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;axelspringer.com/en/inside/the-essentials-what-we-have-adapted-and-why&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW55218471 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply now to begin the next stage of your career at a progressive company that supports both your professional and personal development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of Position&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Awin&#39;s Unlock the Clock (UTC) programme is building the evidence base and infrastructure to move measurement beyond last click, using deterministic, CDN/edge-level signals and advanced data connections from publishers to show the full-funnel and AI-discovery influence that today&#39;s attribution misses. The value of that dataset scales with the quality and scale of the publishers inside it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role exists to acquire and retain those publishers. The Senior Partnerships Manager, Media &amp;amp; Data owns the end-to-end pursuit of medium-to-large global media publications and publisher groups, from first conversation to signature, to live, verified data flowing, and is responsible for building the commercial value exchange that makes Awin the leading partner for a premium publisher to work with. The focus in year one is a small number of flagship, tier-one lighthouse partnerships that prove the model and become the reference cases the rest of the market follows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a new, dedicated role. It is not general publisher account management: the postholder is hired to spearhead these relationships and nothing else.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Land flagship media partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own a global target list of medium-to-large media publications and publisher groups whose audience, content and commerce activity make them high-value contributors to Awin’s deterministic dataset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full pursuit cycle for those targets: identify, qualify, pitch, negotiate, close and hand into onboarding, personally leading senior conversations with commercial, ecommerce, editorial and digital leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver a defined number of tier-one lighthouse partnerships in year one: signed tracking addendum, technically onboarded, and verifiably recording events at agreed volume and quality thresholds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert those wins into reference cases, including case studies, joint narratives and referenceable contacts, that materially shorten the sales cycle for the next tranche of publishers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the publisher value proposition&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and continuously sharpen the answer to “what’s in it for the publisher”: the commercial, editorial and strategic reasons a premium media owner shares CDN and wider data signals with Awin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Construct and negotiate the value exchange, including new revenue lines, advertiser demand, insight and benchmarking, or commercial terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product, Marketing and the workstream owners to translate AI-visibility and full-funnel capability into publisher-facing propositions, collateral and retailer pricing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help each partner build their own value proposition, so the publisher has something new and differentiated to sell to advertisers, not simply a new tag on their site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip partners to sell that proposition through joint collateral, benchmarks, proof points and training for their commercial and editorial teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed publisher objections, commercial expectations and market intelligence back into the project roadmap so the product earns the deals rather than the deals stretching the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the technical and contractual path to live&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the integration conversation with publishes, covering CDN/edge worker or plugin deployment, tag and consent implications, data scope and page performance, with Awin product brought in for deep technical detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the commercial and legal process end to end, including tracking addendum, data-sharing terms, privacy and consent positions, working with Legal and Privacy to reach repeatable rather than bespoke agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold partners accountable to going live and staying live, tracking signed-to-verified-event conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global reach and internal leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate globally from day one across UK, EU and US, coordinating with local Awin market and Publisher Development teams and identified regional representatives rather than duplicating them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the single point of accountability and internal voice for media partner acquisition within the project: represent the workstream in relevant forums and provide clear, honest pipeline and progress reporting to SteerCo level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the advertiser-facing teams so publisher supply and advertiser demand are sequenced together: the data has to be sold on as well as signed up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Awin externally at key industry events, conferences and partner forums to promote Unlock the Clock and Awin’s fuller-funnel measurement strategy to the media community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the playbook: document what works, so the model can be scaled by others and, in time, by a small team reporting into this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success measures (first 12 months)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Signed and live tier-one lighthouse partnerships against an agreed target, evidenced by verified event volume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A qualified, weighted global pipeline of medium-to-large media groups with credible forward visibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A repeatable publisher proposition and commercial framework: not a series of bespoke negotiations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner-facing value propositions live in market, with at least two partners actively selling an Awin-enabled proposition of their own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Referenceable partners willing to advocate publicly, at least one flagship case study in market, and Awin represented on stage at relevant industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measurable advertiser-side pull-through from the partnerships landed, agreed jointly with the advertiser teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in commercial, partnership or account leadership roles, with a significant portion earned publisher-side or media-owner-side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An established personal network of senior contacts across the media and publishing world that can be activated from day one. This is a prerequisite, not a nice-to-have.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience representing an organisation publicly: speaking at industry events, on panels or at partner forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable track record of senior-level relationships inside premium publishers or media groups, including commercial directors, heads of ecommerce, editorial and digital leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating and closing commercial agreements with, or on behalf of, publishers: tenancy, CPC, CPA, fixed fee, data or licensing deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of the affiliate and performance ecosystem and how publishers monetise content, for example Awin, Skimlinks, Rakuten, Partnerize, Impact or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling or landing something new, a product, model or proposition without an established category, rather than managing an existing book of business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating multi-stakeholder deals spanning commercial, editorial, legal, privacy and technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International exposure across at least two of UK, US and DACH/EMEA markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desirable: experience with content licensing, AI/LLM discovery, SEO/AEO, or data partnership deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercially creative, able to construct a value exchange where no price list exists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relationship builder with genuine credibility at senior level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiator, comfortable with ambiguity and long sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent storyteller: can turn technical capability into a publisher-relevant revenue narrative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident, credible public speaker, comfortable on stage and in front of a room as a visible advocate for Awin’s strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starting and resilient. This is a build role, not a maintain role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and low-ego; comfortable pulling in engineering, legal, product and local market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytically confident: fluent in performance data, able to interrogate reporting and defend a number.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic mindset paired with a bias to action and closing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technically literate rather than technical: able to hold a credible conversation about tags, tracking, CDNs and edge/worker deployments, page performance and data flows, and to know when to bring engineering into the room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident with analytics and reporting platforms, including GA4, publisher analytics, BI dashboards and Excel or Sheets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with privacy and consent concepts, including GDPR and consent frameworks, as they affect publisher data sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English essential. German or another European language advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel to relevant markets as required&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
