&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/jW2V5vsMb_k&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are Isar Aerospace and we are at the forefront of New Space building a modern space business to enable faster, better and cheaper access to space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to help democratise space and use it for good in order to improve life on Earth now and for the future generations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a fast-growing company aiming to provide sustainable and environmentally friendly launch solutions for small and medium-sized satellites and constellations into Low Earth Orbit. The company is privately funded by world-leading technology investors with strong commitment and support and our team is made of driven and talented people with a real passion for space innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re making rockets in a way that hasn&#39;t been done before disrupting a traditional industry. If you are up for the challenge, want to work on cutting-edge projects and be part of a team changing the world for better, come, join us and launch your career!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Want to find out more about us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.isaraerospace.com/&quot;&gt;www.isaraerospace.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Protection&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We process your personal data for the purpose of managing the recruitment process and assessing your application. For detailed information on how your data is processed, including your rights, please refer to our &lt;a href=&quot;https://isaraerospace.com/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;DE&quot;&gt;Disclaimer&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;DE&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;Isar Aerospace SE is an equal-opportunity employer committed to fairness and inclusivity. We do not prioritize any specific religion, gender, nationality, or background. Due to security clearance requirements, affiliations with countries listed under § 13 para. 1 no. 17 SÜG may affect the application process. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Brief&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;We deliver the half of the rocket that stays on the ground. As Senior Mechanical Ground Systems Engineer at the Ground Systems department of Isar Aerospace, you will take part in shaping the development of the Ground Systems infrastructure. This includes ground equipment such as the Launch Table, Transporter/Erector, and Hold-Down-Release Mechanism as fundamental parts of the Launchpad, but also the design of equipment for Testing Facilities, R&amp;amp;D, qualification and acceptance of propulsion systems and rocket stages. You will work in close cooperation with other engineering departments as well, such as Propulsion Technology and Launch Vehicle, since their requirements drive the design of the ground support equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Your Role in Our Space Mission:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Reporting directly to the Manager, Mechanical Ground Systems the engineer&#39;s tasks are focused on but not necessarily limited to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Taking responsibility, ownership and accountability for mechanical (sub)systems as part of larger projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Managing requirements proactively between stakeholders for own (sub)systems as part of larger projects and defining Engineering Change Requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Providing technical guidance to and mentor junior/mid-level mechanical ground systems engineers and advising colleagues on matters of design of mechanical/structural ground systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Designing, planning and iterating mechanical and/or structural (sub)systems by means of calculation/CAD tools and numerical simulations&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Creating manufacturing and integration drawings including BOMs for practically manufacturable (sub)systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Performing trade-offs from subsystem level up to entire architectural approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Selecting and procuring suitable hardware for (sub)systems based on requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Be the technical point of contact for externals regarding realization of mechanical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Writing technical documentation, conducting (sub)system design reviews and risk assessments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Evaluating (sub)systems for compliance with environmental and safety regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Planning of commissioning procedures/activities and providing support to operation crews with respect to commissioning activities during commissioning of owned (sub)systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Travel activity to construction and test sites for on-site coordination tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p5&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification Checklist&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;B.Sc./M.Sc. degree in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;7+ years of relevant professional experience in the field of mechanical engineering, aerospace engineering or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;System-level mechanical architecture of complex ground support and launch infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Excellent practical experience with Autodesk Inventor, SolidWorks, Siemens NX or similar 3D CAD software incl. GD&amp;amp;T&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Advanced mechanical design and analysis across structures, mechanisms, pressure systems, fluid interfaces, and dynamic environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of manufacturing, assembly, commissioning and operational constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Excellent analytical skills and ability to apply theoretical knowledge to find practical solutions for engineering challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Adjusting self-sufficiently and quickly to changing work environment and priorities given by management, supporting the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Highly organized, efficient and effective team player with high attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Proactive, open, effective, and constructive communication also in stressful situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Ability of self-criticism and assessing own strengths and weaknesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Role-model for junior engineers, as a technical expert and mentor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;English, fluent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;German, fluent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Knowledge of rocket propulsion technology and/or test facility and launch pad design for aerospace applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Knowledge of mechanical aspects of process plant engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Structural, thermal, vibration analysis experience in Ansys, NASTRAN or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Experience with hydraulic system design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Experience with systems designed for outdoor, ideally offshore environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
